// Geometric loop with conditioning inside the loop body (unnormalised posterior semantics:
// observe(psi) restricts the measure to psi).  Each round the process stops w.p. 1/2; otherwise a
// noisy sensor is queried and we observe that it stayed silent (silent w.p. 4/5).
// The output measure has mass 5/6 < 1, so the exactness criterion of ESOP'26 (Thm. 6) does not apply;
// the finite-mass fixpoint below is exact by Corollary "finite-mass fixpoints are exact".
nat x;
nat c;
nat s;
x := 1;
c := 0;
s := 0;
while (x = 1) {
  {x := 0} [1/2] { c := c + 1; {s := 1} [1/5] {s := 0}; observe(s = 0) }
}
?Pr[c = 3]
?Ex[c]
